From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Nov 2023 13:56:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep WED running until the DMA reset of L1 SER

An L1 recovery stops WED before it stops TX queues. A WED stop turns
off the WED engine that drains WDMA RX rings, while the frame engine
still sends flows to WDMA. The WDMA RX engine then stays busy, and its
reset fails during the DMA reset.

Leave WED running until the DMA reset. That reset closes WDMA ports
first, and WED drains its rings until its own reset. The change comes
from MediaTek SDK commit 303f415b6a79 ("mtk: mt76: mt7996: Remove
wed_stop during L1 SER").

Signed-off-by: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mac.c |    6 ------
 1 file changed, 6 deletions(-)

--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -2801,12 +2801,6 @@ void mt7996_mac_reset_work(struct work_s
 	dev_info(dev->mt76.dev,"==== %s L1 SER recovery start ====",
 		 wiphy_name(hw->wiphy));
 
-	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed_hif2))
-		mtk_wed_device_stop(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed_hif2);
-
-	if (mtk_wed_device_active(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed))
-		mtk_wed_device_stop(&dev->mt76.mmio.wed);
-
 	mt7996_npu_hw_stop(dev);
 	ieee80211_stop_queues(mt76_hw(dev));
 
